TITLE:: RLEDO
summary:: An equal division of the octave as a pitch system, with its val
categories:: Libraries>reLation
related:: Classes/RLPitchSystem, Classes/RLJust, Classes/RLChordSpace, Guides/reLation

DESCRIPTION::
A link::Classes/RLPitchSystem:: whose pitch classes are the Integers code::0..steps-1:: and whose pitches are the Integers (steps from the origin).

Its strong::val:: gives each prime a number of steps: the nearest one, code::(steps * log2(prime)).round::, unless the mapping says otherwise. link::#-interval:: reads a just ratio through the val, so the division knows which of its steps stands for 5/4 or 3/2, and which commas it tempers out (those the val sends to 0).

code::
RLEDO(31).val(3);                  // 49 steps for 3/1, so 18 for a fifth
RLEDO(19).interval([5, 4]);        // 6
RLEDO(12).interval([81, 80]);      // 0: the syntonic comma is tempered out
RLEDO(22).interval([81, 80]);      // 1: not in 22
RLEDO(17).interval([5, 4]);        // 5
RLEDO(17, (5: 40)).interval([5, 4]);   // 6: 17's other major third, by a mapping
RLEDO(19).nearest(11, 1.5);        // 30: the pitch of class 11 closest to an octave and a half up
RLEDO(12).name(10);                // Bb
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
argument:: steps
The number of steps in the octave.
argument:: mapping
nil, or a Dictionary or Event prime -> steps for the primes that do not take their nearest step: code::(5: 40):: gives 5/1 forty steps.

METHOD:: noteNames
The names used in 12 steps.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: steps

METHOD:: val
The steps of a prime: the mapping's, else the nearest.

METHOD:: mapping
The primes the mapping names, with their steps (a copy).

METHOD:: interval
METHOD:: pitchInterval
The steps of a just ratio, reduced to a pitch class (interval) or as a pitch (pitchInterval): code::RLEDO(12).pitchInterval([3, 1]):: is 19.

METHOD:: pcs
Every pitch class, code::[0, 1, ... steps - 1]::.

METHOD:: size
The number of pitch classes.

METHOD:: stepCents
One step in cents.

METHOD:: name
A note name in 12 steps, the step number elsewhere.
